  displayName: "Rumba"
  style: 2
  origin: "Cuba"
  history: "Ballroom Rumba is rooted in Afro-Cuban son and bolero music. Teachers such as Monsieur Pierre (Pierre Lavelle) in London studied dancing in Cuba and helped shape the modern Cuban-style Rumba that was standardized in the 1950s. It is the slowest Latin dance and is often called the dance of love."
  timeSignature: "4/4"
  tempoMinBarsPerMinute: 25
  tempoMaxBarsPerMinute: 27
  difficulty: 3
  characteristics:
  - "Slow and sensual"
  - "Romantic"
  - "Expressive, tells a story"
  - "Counted 2, 3, 4-1"
  skills:
  - "Strong Cuban motion"
  - "Balance and control at slow speed"
  - "Long body lines and extensions"
  - "Connection with your partner"
